  "ch3.say.fast": "Same property order or finished slack tracking keeps <em>FastProperties</em>: fields sit inline right after the 3-word header at fixed byte offsets with zero hash dictionary.",
  "ch3.say.forked": "Merely writing <code>{y, x}</code> instead of <code>{x, y}</code> forked the tree to <em>M4</em>: <code>%HaveSameMap</code> is false and the byte offsets of <code>x</code> and <code>y</code> swapped places.",
  "ch3.say.slack": "Call 1 of <code>new Point()</code> runs with <em>Slack Tracking</em> active: V8 pre-reserves {total} in-object slots ({size64} B) until the construction counter hits zero and shrinks the instance.",
  "ch3.say.dict": "<code>delete</code> kicked the object off the fast path onto a dictionary map ({size64} B shell), dumping properties into an out-of-line <em>NameDictionary</em> hash table.",
  "ch3.limit": "The layout matches host V8 14.6 `%DebugPrint` defaults (object literals starting from `{}` pre-allocate 4 slots; constructor initial maps start with 10). Adding dozens of dynamic fields later overflows into an external `PropertyArray`.",
  "ch4.title": "Inline caches (LoadIC): turning dictionary lookups into one offset load",
  "toc.ch4": "Inline caches: mono, poly & mega",
  "ch4.law": "Hidden classes alone would still leave bytecode searching a `DescriptorArray` on every read. V8 pairs each property access site with a `FeedbackVector` cache slot (`LoadIC`) that remembers the last `Map` and byte offset seen—turning `o.x` into one pointer comparison plus `[rax + offset]`.",
  "ch4.p1": "Inspecting `function getX(o) { return o.x; }` with `%DebugPrint(getX)` exposes the four-stage `LoadProperty` state machine inside `slot #0`: cold code begins `UNINITIALIZED`; after seeing its first shape it turns <strong>`MONOMORPHIC`</strong>, storing one weak `Map` pointer and a `LoadHandler(is in object = 1, field index = ...)` that JIT code compiles to a single guard + offset load; when 2 to <strong>`4` shapes</strong> pass through the same site, it widens into <strong>`POLYMORPHIC`</strong>, scanning a short `WeakFixedArray` guard list up to 4 entries long; as soon as a <strong>5th</strong> shape appears, V8 marks the slot with `megamorphic_symbol` (<strong>`MEGAMORPHIC`</strong>) and drops down to probing a shared global stub hash table. On our Apple arm64 machine over 1,000,000 calls, monomorphic `getX` averaged 1.38 ns per load, whereas crossing past 4 shapes into megamorphic jumped more than 2× to 3.00 ns.",
  "dg.ic.cap": "Figure 4. LoadIC state transitions inside a FeedbackVector slot. Monomorphic holds one Map guard; polymorphic holds 2–4 linear guards; a 5th shape overflows into the megamorphic global hash stub.",
  "dg.ic.aria": "Diagram: FeedbackVector slot transitions from UNINITIALIZED to MONOMORPHIC, POLYMORPHIC up to 4 maps, and MEGAMORPHIC global hash cache",
