  "ch5.limit": "The stepper executes the 5-instruction `addXY` bytecode directly; it omits the cold warm-up phase (the first 7 calls in V8 14.6 before `--invocation-count-for-feedback-allocation=8` allocates the `FeedbackVector`).",
  "ch6.title": "Speculative optimization, OSR & deoptimization bailout",
  "toc.ch6": "Speculative JIT, OSR & deoptimization",
  "ch6.law": "Maglev and TurboFan hit near-C speed by emitting machine code specialized for past observations—guarded by cheap `CheckMaps` and `CheckSmi` checks. When an assumption breaks, V8's deoptimizer rebuilds the Ignition stack frame on the spot and bails out.",
  "ch6.p1": "What if a function is only entered once, yet runs a hot loop? At `JumpLoop`, V8 triggers <strong>OSR (On-Stack Replacement)</strong>—at 100 loop iterations for Maglev or 500 for TurboFan—swapping the live stack frame mid-loop directly into compiled machine code. Inside compiled code, every load is protected by `CheckMaps` and every integer op by `CheckSmi`.",
  "ch6.p2": "Hand an unexpected `{y: 1, x: 2}` to compiled `f(o)` while running `--trace-deopt` on our host Node binary, and V8 logs verbatim: `[bailout (kind: deopt-eager, reason: wrong map)]`. That failed `CheckMaps` guard jumps straight into the <strong>Deoptimizer</strong>, uses compiler metadata to materialize Ignition's exact `BytecodeArray @ 0` frame, `acc`, and registers, widens the `FeedbackVector`, and resumes safely in the interpreter. On a 5,000-call trace, a clean monomorphic run takes ~0.818 ms, whereas one late shape surprise plus recompile lifts it to ~1.151 ms; if shapes keep flipping repeatedly, V8 hits its deopt limit and refuses further optimization (<strong>deopt thrashing</strong>).",
  "dg.deopt.cap": "Figure 6. Speculative guard execution and deoptimization bailout. Passing CheckMaps/CheckSmi stays on native instructions; failing jumps into the Deoptimizer to rebuild the exact Ignition frame.",
  "dg.deopt.aria": "Diagram: compiled JIT guard branching to fast native load on pass vs Deoptimizer and Ignition frame reconstruction on fail",
